# CODEOWNERS — changes to the stable structure require the principal's review.
# Later entries take precedence. Docs: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

# Control layer — read by every session; changes affect everyone
/company/            @Dblackone
/governance/         @Dblackone
/prompts/            @Dblackone
/.claude/            @Dblackone
/.agents/            @Dblackone
/.codex/             @Dblackone
/CLAUDE.md           @Dblackone
/README.md           @Dblackone
/.github/            @Dblackone

# Deploy-critical — Pages must publish only this read-only artifact
/hub/                @Dblackone
/.github/workflows/deploy.yml  @Dblackone
/package.json        @Dblackone

# Financial / client records — append-only, principal-gated
/projects/           @Dblackone
/bim-standards/registers/  @Dblackone

# Cross-model entry pointers — protected like CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md           @Dblackone
/CODEX.md            @Dblackone

# CARVE-OUT — the shared agent report log. Every AI assistant appends to this
# file after every task (governance/agents/GOVERNANCE.md §6), so routing it to
# the principal would put a review on routine bookkeeping. Deliberately owner-
# less: later entries take precedence, so this overrides /governance/ above.
# Append-only by convention — a checker rejects any diff that edits or deletes
# another agent's existing entry.
/governance/agents/REPORT-LOG.md
